{
  "id": "choose-a-visualization-compare-categories", "title": "Compare category counts",
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You'll compare the same measure across two categories in a bar chart." },
    { "type": "section", "id": "compare-bars", "title": "Compare two library counts", "blocks": [
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "navigate", "reftarget": "/d/ktMs4D6Mk/bar-charts-and-pie-charts?viewPanel=15&from=now-1h&to=now&timezone=browser", "verify": "on-page:/d/ktMs4D6Mk", "content": "Open the **Popular JS Frameworks** bar chart." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Each library has a GitHub source repository. Stars let people bookmark a repository or show interest. Forks are copies people can change independently to develop their own version or propose changes. Watchers subscribe to notifications." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Find **Vue** and **React.js**. Compare their green **Github Stars** bars, using the legend to keep the measure the same. Vue's bar is longer in this fixed sample." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "The library names form categories; the star counts supply numeric values. Bar lengths on a shared scale answer \"Which included library has more stars?\" Stars, forks, and watchers measure different actions, not how many people use each library." }
    ] },
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You've compared one numeric measure across categories. Next, read the same star counts as shares of a total." }
  ]
}